course: dictionary
lesson: 9273
title: Words from space science
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Space has no air to breathe, and it is very hot in the sun and very cold in the shade. That is why an astronaut needs a spacesuit. «A spacesuit gives an astronaut air, the right pressure and protection from heat and cold.» So a spacesuit is like a small, safe space you wear.
explain: Use the clues in the sentence. The sentence says what a spacesuit gives: air, the right pressure and protection. Try your meaning in the sentence. If you swap spacesuit for "a T-shirt", the sentence stops making sense, because a T-shirt does not give air.
explain: Spacesuit is made of two smaller words, space and suit. Looking at the parts can help you guess a word's meaning. The dictionary also allows the two-word form, space suit, and both mean the same. Listen for the phrases put on a spacesuit and wear a spacesuit.
fact: A spacesuit is a special suit that an astronaut wears in space.
fact: «A spacesuit gives an astronaut air, the right pressure and protection from heat and cold.»
fact: A spacesuit also protects the astronaut from harmful rays.
fact: Space has no air, so astronauts cannot breathe there without help.
fact: Spacesuit can be written as one word or as two words, space suit, and both mean the same.
exercise: «A spacesuit gives an astronaut air, the right pressure and protection from heat and cold.» What does a spacesuit give an astronaut? | A map of the stars | Loud music to pass the time | Sweets and drinks for the journey | *Air, the right pressure and protection from heat and cold
exercise: In space science lessons, why do astronauts need spacesuits? | Space is full of water to swim in | Spacesuits make them fly faster | Spacesuits are only for fun | *Space has no air, and it is very cold or hot
exercise: Find and copy the two smaller words that make up spacesuit. | *space and suit | sun and time | star and suit | space and sun
test: Which phrase is used with spacesuit in the science lessons? | Read a spacesuit | *Put on a spacesuit | Eat a spacesuit | Sing a spacesuit
test: Why does an astronaut need a spacesuit in space? | To go swimming in the sea | *To get air, the right pressure and protection from heat and cold | To ride a bicycle faster | To carry a heavy bag
exam: «The astronaut stepped out of the ship in her spacesuit.» What is a spacesuit? | A tent for sleeping on the moon | *A special suit that gives air and protection in space | A rocket engine | A type of space food
